            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>A light reflection device comprises a motor and a reflection member having a reflection surface that is formed in a planar shape. The reflection surface reflects incident light. The reflection member performs a revolution and a rotation simultaneously. A direction of the revolution of the reflection member and a direction of the rotation of the reflection member are the same. The motor drives the reflection member so that the angular velocity of the revolution of the reflection member is equal to twice angular velocity of the rotation of the reflection member.</p>
            </abstract>
